Dear 3D ADEPT Editorial Team,

Solidon3D 0.2.2 offers a software story at the intersection of AM workflow,
data control and AI governance: the language model is an optional interface to
a fixed operation API, not a geometry engine.

Every model change is a registered, parameterised operation evaluated by
deterministic geometry code. The same operation can be requested from a menu,
shortcut or chat. The model cannot execute source code, and executable code is
never embedded in a project file. Reusable custom components travel as recipes
of registered operations and values.

Version 0.2.2 applies that architecture to practical preparation tasks:

* recognised holes in imported STL or 3MF can be resized on their original
  axis;
* standards-based inserts, fastener seats and bearing seats can use fit values
  measured from a printed calibration artefact;
* physical filament spools carry their own process data into the correct 3MF
  material slot and external slicer;
* cloud and local model settings state clearly which data leaves the machine.

All modelling, analysis and export remain available without AI, an account or
an internet connection. Solidon runs on Windows, macOS and Linux and keeps
project files local.

Product: https://solidon3d.de/en/
Changelog: https://solidon3d.de/en/changelog.html

I can provide the released 0.2.2 build, an architecture note, a safe project
file example and the resulting STL-to-3MF workflow for editorial review.

